        "model_answer": "1. Latency period: IgA Nephropathy is 'synpharyngitic' (occurs concurrently or within 1-3 days of mucosal URTI/GI infection), whereas PSGN occurs 1-3 weeks after strep pharyngitis or 3-6 weeks after impetigo; 2. Complement levels: Serum C3 is NORMAL in IgA Nephropathy, whereas C3 is LOW (consumed) in PSGN; 3. Recurrence: IgA Nephropathy causes recurrent episodic gross haematuria with mucosal infections.",
