        "model_answer": "Murine typhus is caused by Rickettsia typhi, transmitted by the rat flea (Xenopsylla cheopis) in urban/warehouse/port settings, and rarely produces an eschar (<5%). Scrub typhus is caused by Orientia tsutsugamushi, transmitted by trombiculid chigger mites in rural/jungle scrub (e.g., Tekong), and classically produces a pathognomonic black necrotic eschar.",
