        "question": "What are the ECG and physical examination hallmarks of Complete (3rd-Degree) Heart Block, and what causes 'cannon A waves'?",
        "prompt": "What are the ECG and physical examination hallmarks of Complete (3rd-Degree) Heart Block, and what causes 'cannon A waves'?",
        "model_answer": "ECG hallmarks: 1) Regular P-P interval (atrial rate > ventricular rate), 2) Regular R-R interval (slow escape rhythm, 30-40 bpm), 3) Complete AV dissociation (variable PR intervals with P waves marching right through QRS complexes). Physical signs: Bradycardia, variable intensity of first heart sound (S1), and intermittent giant 'cannon A waves' in the JVP—caused whenever the right atrium contracts against a closed tricuspid valve during simultaneous ventricular systole.",
