        "prompt": "Outline your immediate emergency management in the resuscitation bay and definitive therapy.",
        "model_answer": "1. Apply defibrillator/transcutaneous pacing pads immediately; 2. Trial IV Atropine 500 mcg bolus (up to 3mg), though note that wide-complex infra-Hisian (Mobitz II / 3rd degree) block rarely responds to Atropine (which acts at the AV node); 3. Start immediate Transcutaneous Pacing (with IV analgesia/sedation) or IV Isoprenaline/Adrenaline infusion (2-10 mcg/min) to maintain HR >60 and perfusion; 4. Exclude reversible causes (Drugs: beta-blockers/CCB/digoxin; Electrolytes: hyperkalaemia; Ischaemia: inferior STEMI); 5. Definitive: Cardiology insertion of a Permanent Dual-Chamber Pacemaker (DDD PPM).",
        "target_rubric": "1. Apply defibrillator/transcutaneous pacing pads immediately; 2. Trial IV Atropine 500 mcg bolus (up to 3mg), though note that wide-complex infra-Hisian (Mobitz II / 3rd degree) block rarely responds to Atropine (which acts at the AV node); 3. Start immediate Transcutaneous Pacing (with IV analgesia/sedation) or IV Isoprenaline/Adrenaline infusion (2-10 mcg/min) to maintain HR >60 and perfusion; 4. Exclude reversible causes (Drugs: beta-blockers/CCB/digoxin; Electrolytes: hyperkalaemia; Ischaemia: inferior STEMI); 5. Definitive: Cardiology insertion of a Permanent Dual-Chamber Pacemaker (DDD PPM).",
