        "model_answer": "In HOCM, dynamic LVOT obstruction is caused by the hypertrophied septum and Systolic Anterior Motion (SAM) of the mitral valve leaflet. Manoeuvres that DECREASE LV cavity volume/preload (Valsalva strain phase, standing up from squatting, nitrates, dehydration) bring the septum and mitral leaflet closer together -> HOCM murmur becomes LOUDER (whereas Aortic Stenosis becomes softer). Manoeuvres that INCREASE LV volume/preload or afterload (passive leg raise, squatting, isometric handgrip) push the septum and leaflet apart -> HOCM murmur becomes SOFTER.",
