        "question": "Outline your immediate management plan for Thyroid Storm (Decompensated Thyrotoxicosis).",
        "prompt": "Outline your immediate management plan for Thyroid Storm (Decompensated Thyrotoxicosis).",
        "model_answer": "5 Bs of Thyroid Storm Management: 1. Block beta-adrenergic effects: IV/PO Propranolol (60-80mg q4h; also inhibits peripheral T4->T3 conversion) or IV Esmolol; 2. Block hormone synthesis: Loading Propylthiouracil (PTU 500-1000mg PO/NG, preferred in storm & 1st trimester as it blocks T4->T3) or Carbimazole; 3. Block peripheral T4->T3 & cover adrenal reserve: IV Hydrocortisone 100mg q8h; 4. Block hormone release: Lugol's Iodine given >= 1 HOUR AFTER PTU; 5. Active cooling + Paracetamol (STRICTLY AVOID Aspirin/Salicylates as they displace T4/T3 from Thyroid-Binding Globulin!) + IV fluids + ICU.",
