        "prompt": "Outline your immediate management plan for Acute Ileocolic Intussusception.",
        "model_answer": "1. NBM + NG tube decompression + IV fluid resuscitation (20 mL/kg 0.9% NaCl bolus) + Paediatric Surgery team standby; 2. First-line treatment (if NO peritonitis/free air/shock): Ultrasound/fluoroscopy-guided Pneumatic (Air) Enema Reduction (>85% success rate); 3. Contraindications to enema (perforation/peritonitis/hemodynamic instability or failed enema) -> Emergency Laparotomy/Laparoscopy (manual reduction from distal to proximal like squeezing a toothpaste tube, or bowel resection if necrotic).",
