        "question": "What defines a Complex Febrile Seizure (vs Simple), and how do you counsel anxious parents regarding recurrence and epilepsy risk?",
        "prompt": "What defines a Complex Febrile Seizure (vs Simple), and how do you counsel anxious parents regarding recurrence and epilepsy risk?",
        "model_answer": "A febrile seizure is COMPLEX if ANY of the following apply: 1. Focal onset/features; 2. Prolonged duration > 15 minutes; 3. Multiple recurrences (>=2 episodes) within 24 hours. Parental counselling: Simple febrile seizures cause NO brain damage or intellectual decline; recurrence risk is ~30% during future fevers until age 5; lifetime epilepsy risk is ~1-2% (barely above the 1% general population baseline).",
