        "prompt": "Outline your immediate management plan for Simple Febrile Convulsion Secondary to Acute Otitis Media.",
        "model_answer": "1. Treat the underlying source of fever (Amoxicillin for Acute Otitis Media + Paracetamol/Ibuprofen for comfort — note antipyretics improve comfort but do NOT prevent febrile seizure recurrence); 2. Do NOT perform routine LP, EEG, neuroimaging, or prescribe long-term anticonvulsants for a Simple Febrile Seizure; 3. Parent education on seizure first aid: place child in lateral recovery position, time the seizure, never put anything in the mouth, call 995 if seizure lasts >5 minutes.",
