        "prompt": "Outline your immediate management plan for Delirium Tremens (Severe Alcohol Withdrawal) with Wernicke's Encephalopathy Risk.",
        "model_answer": "1. Immediate High-Dose Parenteral Thiamine (IV Pabrinex 2 pairs TDS for 3-5 days) given BEFORE any glucose solution; 2. First-line symptom-triggered/front-loaded Benzodiazepine regimen: IV/PO Diazepam or Chlordiazepoxide (or **Lorazepam** in liver cirrhosis/impaired hepatic metabolism, since Lorazepam undergoes direct glucuronidation with no active metabolites!); 3. Correct severe Hypomagnesemia (Mg2+ 0.48) and Hypokalemia (Mg is required for thiamine activity and lowers seizure threshold).",
